Description: Outlook-style upcoming-event reminder modal for Linux
 An Outlook-style upcoming-event reminder modal for Linux (GNOME / Wayland).
 .
 A small background daemon polls your calendars and, when events approach,
 pops a true modal window listing everything that's currently due. Each
 event can be dismissed, snoozed (with a context-aware dropdown), or joined
 when an online meeting link is detected.
 .
 Features:
  - Scrollable list of due events in a modal window
  - Per-event Dismiss and Snooze with context-aware dropdown
  - Per-event Join for Microsoft Teams, Google Meet, and Zoom links
  - Dismiss all footer button
  - Pluggable calendar backends: ICS, Microsoft Graph, Google Calendar
